396. Rotate Function

You are given an integer array nums of length n.

Assume arrk to be an array obtained by rotating nums by k positions clock-wise. We define the rotation function F on nums as follow:

F(k) = 0 * arrk[0] + 1 * arrk[1] + ... + (n - 1) * arrk[n - 1].
Return the maximum value of F(0), F(1), ..., F(n-1).

The test cases are generated so that the answer fits in a 32-bit integer.

 
Example 1:

Input: nums = [4,3,2,6]
Output: 26
Explanation:
F(0) = (0 * 4) + (1 * 3) + (2 * 2) + (3 * 6) = 0 + 3 + 4 + 18 = 25
F(1) = (0 * 6) + (1 * 4) + (2 * 3) + (3 * 2) = 0 + 4 + 6 + 6 = 16
F(2) = (0 * 2) + (1 * 6) + (2 * 4) + (3 * 3) = 0 + 6 + 8 + 9 = 23
F(3) = (0 * 3) + (1 * 2) + (2 * 6) + (3 * 4) = 0 + 2 + 12 + 12 = 26
So the maximum value of F(0), F(1), F(2), F(3) is F(3) = 26.
Example 2:

Input: nums = [100]
Output: 0
 

Constraints:

n == nums.length
1 <= n <= 10^5
-100 <= nums[i] <= 100

APPROACH 1 : BRUTE FORCE :
            NESTED LOOP WE WILL USE.
            inside outer loop first we will rotate array clockwise then in another loop we will find f(x) by multiplying arr[i]*i and summing them . 
            TC: o(n^2)   will give TLE.

APPROACH 2 : SIMULATION 
            so basically here i will find f(0) and f(1) with that only we will be able to find a formula with which we will do it in TC: O(n).
             nums = [4,3,2,6]
            F(0) = (0 * 4) + (1 * 3) + (2 * 2) + (3 * 6) = 0 + 3 + 4 + 18 = 25
            F(1) = (0 * 6) + (1 * 4) + (2 * 3) + (3 * 2) = 0 + 4 + 6 + 6 = 16

            F(k) = 0*a0 + 1*a1 + 2*a2 + 3*a3 + .................. + (n-2)*an-2 + (n-1)*an-1;
            F(k+1) = 1*a0 + 2*a1 + 3*a2 + 4*a3 + .................. + (n-1)*an-2 + 0*an-1;

          F(k+1) - F(k) = a0 + a1 + a2 + a3 + a4 + ........ + an-2 - (n-1)*an-1; 
          F(k+1) - F(k) = a0 + a1 + a2 + a3 + a4 + ........ + an-2 - n*an-1 + an-1; 
          F(k+1) - F(k) = a0 + a1 + a2 + a3 + a4 + ........ + an-2 + an-1 - n&an-1;
          F(k+1) - F(k) = sum of all elements of array - n*an-1;   HERE an-1 ==> representing the last element in the rotated array which we will find using (n-i-1);

           F(k+1) = F(k) + sum of all elements of array - n*an-1; 


CODE : 
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int maxRotateFunction(vector<int>& nums) {
    int n = nums.size();

    int sum = 0;
    int f = 0;

    // Calculate sum and F(0)
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        sum += nums[i];
        f += i * nums[i];
    }

    int maxi = f;

    // Calculate remaining rotations
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        int newF = f + sum - (n * nums[n - i - 1]);
        f = newF;
        maxi = max(maxi, newF);
    }

    return maxi;
}
         
